From: VLCKit Aloha Release <devnull@alohabrowser.com>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] apple/build.conf: disable rav1e on iOS

rav1e is a Rust-based AV1 encoder. iOS VLCKit is a playback engine — it
decodes AV1 via dav1d, never encodes — so rav1e is dead weight here.

Building rav1e pulls in cargo-c, which in turn compiles the `time` crate
from source. On both nightly and current stable Rust the bundled cargo-c
version chokes with E0282 (type annotations needed for Box<_>), breaking
the entire contrib build mid-way. Dropping rav1e from the contrib graph
sidesteps the toolchain incompatibility entirely.
---
 extras/package/apple/build.conf | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/extras/package/apple/build.conf b/extras/package/apple/build.conf
index 0000000..1111111 100644
--- a/extras/package/apple/build.conf
+++ b/extras/package/apple/build.conf
@@ -90,6 +90,7 @@ export VLC_CONTRIB_OPTIONS_MACOSX=(
 # Additional contrib bootstrap options for iOS
 export VLC_CONTRIB_OPTIONS_IOS=(
     --disable-aom
+    --disable-rav1e
 )

 # Additional contrib bootstrap options for tvOS
